an></span>
<span id="cb48-4"><a href="#cb48-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:codecResource=</span><span class="st">&quot;MPEG Audio Version 1 Layer 3&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb48-5"><a href="#cb48-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:formatResource=</span><span class="st">&quot;audio/mpeg&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb48-6"><a href="#cb48-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        http://media.slub-dresden.de/fon/snp/a/012100/fon_snp_a_012100_01.mp3</span>
<span id="cb48-7"><a href="#cb48-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:linkResource</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb48-8"><a href="#cb48-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:resourceRepresentation</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.4" id="encodinganalog"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.4</span> <span
            class="citation"
            data-cites="encodingAnalog">@encodingAnalog</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#encodinganalog">lido:encodinganalog</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for many LIDO elements
            to record the field label in the source database from which
            the element content was migrated. The source format for the
            whole document is indicated in the attribute <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#relatedencoding"><em>lido:relatedencoding</em></a>
            of the <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#lidoWrap">LIDO
            Wrapper</a>.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            contains the popular French title for <em>Mona Lisa</em>,
            “La Joconde”, stored in the source database as “titre
            d’usage” under the field label “Type de titre”. The title
            type is indexed with the AAT descriptor ‘<a
            href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300417200">popular
            title</a>’.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb49"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb49-1"><a href="#cb49-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:titleSet</span></span>
<span id="cb49-2"><a href="#cb49-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300417200&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb49-3"><a href="#cb49-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:appellationValue</span></span>
<span id="cb49-4"><a href="#cb49-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:pref=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00170&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb49-5"><a href="#cb49-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:encodinganalog=</span><span class="st">&quot;Type de titre&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb49-6"><a href="#cb49-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:label=</span><span class="st">&quot;titre d&#39;usage&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb49-7"><a href="#cb49-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;fr&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb49-8"><a href="#cb49-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        La Joconde</span>
<span id="cb49-9"><a href="#cb49-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:appellationValue</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb49-10"><a href="#cb49-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:sourceAppellation</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb49-11"><a href="#cb49-11" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &quot;Institut national d&#39;histoire de l&#39;art, Portrait de Lisa Gherardini. URL: https://agorha.inha.fr/ark:/54721/8e279ee1-f842-4eb3-994d-797ca8562c09</span>
<span id="cb49-12"><a href="#cb49-12" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:sourceAppellation</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb49-13"><a href="#cb49-13" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:titleSet</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.5" id="formatresource"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.5</span> <span
            class="citation"
            data-cites="formatResource">@formatResource</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#formatResource">lido:formatResource</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for elements referring
            to the internet media type of a web resource, i.e., &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#legalBodyWeblink">lido:legalBodyWeblink</a>&gt;,
            &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#linkResource">lido:linkResource</a>&gt;,
            &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectWebResource">lido:objectWebResource</a>&gt;,
            and &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordInfoLink">lido:recordInfoLink</a>&gt;.
            It is recommended to use the <a
            href="https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml">IANA
            Media Types</a> as values.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            marks the format of the Web resource for a study of the
            <em>Mona Lisa</em> as “text/html” according to the IANA
            Media Type.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb50"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb50-1"><a href="#cb50-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:object</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb50-2"><a href="#cb50-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:objectWebResource</span></span>
<span id="cb50-3"><a href="#cb50-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:formatResource=</span><span class="st">&quot;text/html&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb50-4"><a href="#cb50-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;de&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb50-5"><a href="#cb50-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        http://foto.biblhertz.it/obj08012138</span>
<span id="cb50-6"><a href="#cb50-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:objectWebResource</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb50-7"><a href="#cb50-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:object</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.6" id="geographicalentity"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.6</span> <span
            class="citation"
            data-cites="geographicalEntity">@geographicalEntity</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#geographicalEntity">lido:geographicalEntity</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#partOfPlace">lido:partOfPlace</a>&gt;,
            &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#place">lido:place</a>&gt;,
            &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#repositoryLocation">lido:repositoryLocation</a>&gt;,
            and &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#vitalPlaceActor">lido:vitalPlaceActor</a>&gt;
            to indicate the kind of place as a physical entity, such as
            a <em>forest</em> or a <em>river</em>. This attribute was
            intended in LIDO v1.0 to qualify th